Item 00 (toolchain and skeleton) is done, and the gate passes. Nothing was committed or pushed, and `chez_scheme/original/` is unchanged.

- **Toolchain:** everything needed is installed. Racket is v8.18 CS and `racket/gui` loads; Chez Scheme 10.0.0 is available as both `scheme` and `chezscheme`.
- **Skeleton:** I added `racket/info.rkt`, a stub `racket/main.rkt` (GPL header plus a "ported to Racket" line), `chez_scheme/oracle/README.md`, `docs/porting-notes.md` and `docs/divergences.md`. For now, `racket racket/main.rkt` just prints that the GUI isn't implemented yet.
- **`tests/run-tests.sh`:** it runs `raco test racket/` and then every Chez check in `chez_scheme/oracle/tests/`, stopping at the first failure. It also fails if there are no Chez checks at all. I confirmed it exits 1 when a deliberately failing check is present.
- **Tests, written first:**
  - `racket/tests/skeleton-test.rkt`: failed with "cannot open module file … main.rkt" before the stub existed, and passes now.
  - `chez_scheme/oracle/tests/reader-check.ss`: checks the Chez version is 10 and that Chez can read all 45 `.ss` files in the original (1454 top-level forms). It tests the environment and the original rather than new code, so it passed from the start.
- **`docs/code-map.md`:** one paragraph per original file, covering what it defines, what it depends on, its line count and whether it uses SWL. It also has a section of general facts for the port: the `tell` object system, every random-number entry point and which files draw from it, how sorting and tables work, and Chez functions the original redefines.

Things I found that differ from what TASK.md says (recorded in the code map and PROGRESS.md):
- Toolkit calls also appear in three files TASK.md doesn't list: `utilities.ss`, `workspace-graphics.ss` and `theme-graphics.ss`.
- There is no `weighted-pick` in the original; the equivalent is called `stochastic-pick`.
- `constants.ss` also makes random draws.
- `metacat.ss` needs `*platform*`, `*metacat-directory*` and `*file-dialog-directory*` to be defined. They're commented out in the distribution, so the oracle prelude will have to provide them.

I marked the item `[x]` in `iterations.md` and set PROGRESS.md to 1/18 SOLVED with an Iteration 1 section. Seventeen items remain, so I didn't add LOOP_COMPLETE.

